# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Order matters: Pages serves the first match, so the catch-all must be LAST or
# it swallows every real file. That is what was happening before — /robots.txt,
# /og.png and every mistyped URL returned the homepage with a 200, which turns
# each one into another duplicate of the homepage in Google's index.
#
# Turn OFF the dashboard's "Single Page Application" setting when deploying, or
# it reinstates its own catch-all above these rules.
#
# Note: Pages cannot match on query strings, so the legacy `/?problem=<slug>`
# deep links are redirected in the app instead (see src/App.tsx).

# All 66 pages are real files on disk — nothing here is an SPA route any more,
# so anything that falls through genuinely does not exist. 404, not 200.
/*    /404.html    404
